(3)  183/   88DB4 :                     	; These first three notes are too high when combined with this track's
(3)  184/   88DB4 :                     	; transposition value, causing them to overflow the PSG frequency table
(3)  185/   88DB4 :                     	; and play invalid notes. In the Sonic 1 prototype, this problem was
(3)  186/   88DB4 :                     	; even worse as there were smpsChangeTransposition commands around the
(3)  187/   88DB4 :                     	; following line that raised the notes yet another octave higher,
(3)  188/   88DB4 :                     	; causing the fourth note to break too.
(3)  189/   88DB4 :                     	; Since the commands are gone now, we can assume that this was the
(3)  190/   88DB4 :                     	; developers' intended solution, though it unfortunately only fixed the
(3)  191/   88DB4 :                     	; fourth note. So, in order to fix the bug for good, the notes on the
(3)  192/   88DB4 :                     	; following line have to be lowered by yet another octave.
(3)  193/   88DB4 :                     	;dc.b	nRst, $06, nE5, $03, $03, $06, nRst, nE4, $24
(3)  194/   88DB4 : 8006 B503 0306      	dc.b	nRst, $06, nE4, $03, $03, $06, nRst, nE3, $24 ; Fixed
            88DBA : 80A9 24          
