(2)    2/   8D6F6 :                     ; SFX metadata (pointers, priorities, flags)
(2)    3/   8D6F6 :                     
(2)    4/   8D6F6 :                     ; Priority of sound. New music or SFX must have a priority higher than or equal
(2)    5/   8D6F6 :                     ; to what is stored in v_sndprio or it won't play. If bit 7 of new priority is
(2)    6/   8D6F6 :                     ; set ($80 and up), the new music or SFX will not set its priority -- meaning
(2)    7/   8D6F6 :                     ; any music or SFX can override it (as long as it can override whatever was
(2)    8/   8D6F6 :                     ; playing before). Usually, SFX will only override SFX, special SFX ($D0-$DF)
(2)    9/   8D6F6 :                     ; will only override special SFX and music will only override music.
(2)   10/   8D6F6 :                     ; Of course, this isn't the case anymore, as priorities no longer apply to
(2)   11/   8D6F6 :                     ; special SFX or music.
(2)   12/   8D6F6 :                     ; TODO Maybe I should make it apply to Special SFX, too.
(2)   13/   8D6F6 :                     ; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
